 "_comment": "sounds.json - every sound effect the game plays by name through Scripts/sfx.gd (Sfx.play(\"weapon_hit\") ...). files: one is picked at random each time. target: how loud that kind of sound should be (LUFS) - tools/balance_sounds.py measures the files and writes volume_db to reach it, so every sound sits at a consistent level whatever its file's own loudness (re-run it after adding or replacing a file). Optional: loop (keeps playing until stopped), max_seconds (plays only the start, with a short fade), start (skip silence at the start, seconds), pitch (random pitch change each play, e.g. 0.08 = +/-8%, so repeats don't sound identical), positional (heard from where it happens in the world rather than in your ears). music: every music track (by path) with the same target/volume_db balancing; Scripts/global_background_music.gd plays each at its volume_db.",
